-### Training Objective
-The network parameters are optimized by minimizing the mean squared error (L2 loss) between the rendered images $\hat{I}$ and the ground-truth training images $I$ [S3, unofficial][S9, S26][S29, unofficial]:
-$$
-\mathcal{L} = \frac{1}{|R|} \sum_{\mathbf{r} \in R} \|\hat{C}(\mathbf{r}) - C(\mathbf{r})\|_2^2
-$$
-where $R$ is the set of rays sampled from the training images [S7][S29, unofficial]. The total loss includes contributions from both the coarse and fine networks [S4]:
-$$
-\mathcal{L} = \sum_{\mathbf{r}} \left[ \|\hat{C}_{\text{coarse}}(\mathbf{r}) - C(\mathbf{r})\|_2^2 + \|\hat{C}_{\text{fine}}(\mathbf{r}) - C(\mathbf{r})\|_2^2 \right]
-$$
-
-### Pseudocode
+*   $T_i = \exp\left(-\sum_{j=1}^{i-1} \sigma_j \delta_j\right)$ is the accumulated transmittance (probability of the ray passing through previous segments without interaction) [S4, S9][S15, unofficial].
+*   The term $\alpha_i = 1 - \exp(-\sigma_i \delta_i)$ is the opacity of segment $i$.
+
+**Training:**
+The network parameters $\Theta$ are optimized by minimizing the Mean Squared Error (MSE) between the rendered image $\hat{I}$ and the ground-truth image $I$ [S3, S6, unofficial]:
+$$
+\mathcal{L} = \frac{1}{|R|} \sum_{\mathbf{r} \in R} \|\hat{C}(\mathbf{r}) - C(\mathbf{r})\|^2
+$$
+where $R$ is a batch of rays sampled from the training images [S9, S34].
